  "chunking": {
    "method": "auto",
    "chunkSize": 200,
    "maxSize": 200,
    "minSize": 100,
    "overlap": 24,
    "language": "english",
    "$comment": "Studio reads different keys on the two ingest paths: lib/kb/ingest.ts::selectChunker reads chunkSize/overlap, lib/knowledge/documents/{service.ts::processDocumentAsync,embed-pipeline.ts::planDocumentEmbedding} read maxSize/overlap/minSize. All are set to the same numbers here so the paths are comparable. Studio's own defaults are NOT one set of numbers: the knowledge_base.chunking_config column defaults to {\"maxSize\": 1024, \"minSize\": 1, \"overlap\": 200} (packages/db/schema.ts:2644), which is what a UI-created KB stores, while the code fallbacks are chunkSize 1024 / overlap 128 (lib/kb/ingest.ts) and maxSize 1024 / minSize 100 / overlap 200 (service.ts, embed-pipeline.ts) — so a UI-created KB and a code-defaulted KB disagree on minSize (1 vs 100) and, on the ingest.ts path, on overlap (200 vs 128). The `defaults` knowledge base below freezes the column-default shape. The other three shrink the numbers so a 12-document corpus crosses the 50-chunk clustering cold start."
  },
  "knowledgeBases": [
    {
      "key": "hybrid",
      "engine": "v2-hybrid",
      "ingestVia": "lib/knowledge/documents/service.ts::processDocumentAsync",
      "chunking": "fixture",
      "kmeansK": 8,
      "$comment": "The inline (non-BullMQ) ingestion fallback. Writes the shared `embedding` table (tags inherited from the document) and the per-KB vector partition with the same row ids, then extracts keywords inline. The nine v2 hybrid queries and the v1 tag+vector query run here."
    },
    {
      "key": "bullmq",
      "engine": "v2-hybrid",
      "ingestVia": "lib/knowledge/documents/embed-pipeline.ts::planDocumentEmbedding -> processEmbedBatch -> finalizeDocumentEmbedding -> lib/kb/jobs/keywords-extract.ts::handleKeywordsExtract",
      "chunking": "fixture",
      "kmeansK": 8,
      "$comment": "The production worker path (worker/processors/knowledge.ts:92-117 dispatches exactly these four jobs). Same corpus as `hybrid`. Has no queries of its own: the suite replays every `hybrid` query against it and asserts identical corpus counts and identical top-5s, which is what proves the resumable fan-out and the inline fallback agree."
    },
    {
      "key": "sdk",
      "engine": "v2-partition-only",
      "ingestVia": "lib/kb/ingest.ts::ingestDocument",
      "chunking": "fixture",
      "kmeansK": 8,
      "$comment": "The SDK / runtime-route / kb_add_file block path. Writes ONLY the per-KB vector partition, with freshly generated chunk ids that do not exist in the shared `embedding` table — so its keyword vocabulary stays empty for good (see fixtures/README.md, \"Known defects carried deliberately\"). It is also the only path that writes caller `metadata` into the partition (ingest.ts:332), which is why the metadata-filter probe lives here."
    },
    {
      "key": "defaults",
      "engine": "v2-partition-only",
      "ingestVia": "lib/kb/ingest.ts::ingestDocument",
      "chunking": "studio-column-default",
      "kmeansK": 8,
      "$comment": "Same path as `sdk`, but the knowledge_base row is inserted WITHOUT a chunking_config so the column default applies — the shape every UI-created KB actually has. At those numbers each fixture document is a single chunk (12 chunks total), which also puts the read path below the 50-chunk clustering cold start: no clusters, no cluster routing, and retrieval is effectively whole-document."
    }
  ],
